<p><strong>The best way for a salon or beauty parlour in Nepal to take bookings without phone calls is a booking system that lets clients book online by branch, service and stylist, refuses double-bookings, and records every payment against the booking. Zennly does this across multiple branches.</strong></p>

<p>Most salons and beauty parlours in Nepal still run on the same three tools: a paper appointment book, phone calls and WhatsApp messages. It works until a stylist is double-booked, a regular turns up to find her slot given away, or the owner cannot tell what a branch earned yesterday.</p>
<h2>Why the appointment book breaks down</h2>
<p>A paper book shows one person&rsquo;s view of the day. It does not tell the second branch what the first one promised, it cannot stop two people booking the same stylist, and it cannot answer calls at 10 pm. As soon as you have more than one chair filling up, the gaps show.</p>
<h2>What a salon booking system should do</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Let clients book online</strong> &ndash; pick a branch, a service and a time, and get a booking number back.</li>
<li><strong>Schedule by stylist</strong> &ndash; so the right person is always attached to the right service.</li>
<li><strong>Refuse clashes</strong> &ndash; a slot that is taken stays taken, across every branch.</li>
<li><strong>Track payments</strong> &ndash; cash, card and online recorded against each booking.</li>
<li><strong>Control discounts</strong> &ndash; requests approved by a manager, with a record.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Managing stylists across branches</h2>
<p>Stylists often work at more than one location. Scheduling a transfer in advance, instead of texting the branch manager, keeps both branches&rsquo; calendars accurate. See how <a href="/features/staff-management/">staff scheduling and transfers</a> work.</p>
<h2>Start with the basics</h2>
<p>You do not need to change everything at once. Many salons begin with online booking and payment tracking, then add discount approval and reports. <a href="/solutions/salon/">See how Zennly works for salons and beauty parlours</a>.</p>

<h2>Salon booking in Nepal: what to plan for</h2>
<p>Many salons and beauty parlours in Kathmandu, Lalitpur and Pokhara get their busiest days around the Dashain and Tihar festivals and the wedding season. Those are the days a paper book fails first. Set up stylists, services and prices before the rush, and let clients book online so the phone line is free for exceptions.</p>
